{
  "slug": "artist:eazy-e",
  "name": "Eazy-E",
  "editorial_article": "Born Eric Lynn Wright in Compton, California, Eazy-E founded the foundational hip hop group N.W.A in 1986. His debut solo album Eazy-Duz-It, released in 1988, reached number 41 on the Billboard 200 and eventually moved over 2.5 million copies in the United States by 1994. The 1993 EP It's On (Dr. Dre) 187um Killa peaked at number five on the Billboard 200 and remains the only hip hop EP to achieve multi-platinum status. His final studio album, the posthumous Str8 off tha Streetz of Muthaphukkin Compton, reached number three on the Billboard 200 in 1995. Throughout his career, he released music through labels including Ruthless Records, Priority Records, Relativity Records, and Epic Records.",
